		<td width="100%">
			<table width="100%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="2" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%" class="title" colspan="2">Why our first raid failed</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3548">olthar</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/3/2002 - 5:39 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2836">Olthar Othlinden</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2837">Tylendil</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														well our first raid was a flop, reasons why it was?... <br />
A: we didn't have enough people						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3111">ktadema</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/3/2002 - 11:46 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2488">Givins Ntakhiens</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2861">Felious Gudlious</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2487">Izzek Krakumheads</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Actually, I thought we had a decent little turnout.  How many did we have out there, 18?  I think that's about right.  Not to mention we had at least 3 non guildies at times in groups.  That's not a bad turn out, I don't think.  Mistmoore isn't like the Plane of Fear where you need 4 groups to take the zone.  One good group can do a lot of damage to Mistmoore, if the group has high enough levels.  There might be our problem.  We might not have QUITE enough exp. for MM.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3111">ktadema</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/3/2002 - 11:48 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2488">Givins Ntakhiens</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2861">Felious Gudlious</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2487">Izzek Krakumheads</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Here's another thought!  Almost eveyone in our guild has been getting XP via the LOIL, FM, DL path.  All outdoor dungeons.  Maybe we need to be working on our dungeon skills, where snaring/rooting mobs and mezzing is critical.  Our little guild might not have been practicing the right skills to learn to control dungeons.  I'm not saying this is the case, but just a possibility.  I throw this out there because there was a whole lot of training going on.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3681">ntadema</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/4/2002 - 12:38 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2958">Chintzy Eatstumuch</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I have to say, I found this raid extraordinarily depressing.  Splitting the under 34 groups into two teams of four was not a good idea.  If that looks like its going to happen next time, I'll volunteer to drop out so a decent 6-man group can be made.  In fact, I think I'm gonna wait to see what the turnout is before I even show to the next raid.  <br />
<br />
Also, the high levels are gonna need to watch their trains cause they're wiping EVERYBODY out.  <br />
<br />
And one more thing: if you're going to participate in these raids, please bind nearby...Dying is a miserable experience enough without having to wait for members of your group to run across 4 zones.<br />
<br />
And ANOTHER thing:  the organization process was WAY too timeconsuming.  Took a friggin hour to get groups together.  AAnd then we get wiped in about 2 milliseconds.  <br />
<br />
Tonight was one of my worst EQ playing experiences in a looong time.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3548">olthar</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/4/2002 - 9:25 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2836">Olthar Othlinden</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2837">Tylendil</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														heh, your right, we have been messing up our dungeon expierience with all of our time in places like LOIO, FM, OT and DL. I don't know about others, but some of us have spent times in other dungeons like Guk, and Unrest. We did have a nice turnout for the event, 15 was the most on at once I believe, with a total of 19 or so guildies in and out throughout the raid. We also at the peak had 3 non guildies in it. The splitting of the lower group would have worked out if eithe group was more condensed in levels, we had 6 level 28's a 25 a 20 and 3 30's so it was a bit odd, hopefully by our next raid the levels will be more condensed. I also think that as a guild we were not large enough to take on MistMoore, when Dragons Fist did mistmoore (when we had meeting) there was a group at ent, 2 in graveyard (none in pit where we went) one in the ent of castle (where we stalled out) and then 2 more groups further in, one in the courtyard and one at xotyl (spelled wrong). Sorry about the trains that wiped out the lower groups. The wolf group was working out until our train wiped them out. If we had been able to clear the zone of the out of place castle spawns before the wolf and bear groups went back in they would have had a long and successful 2nd attempt at the raid, because we didn't train until that horrible end. Our meeting will be mostly about the raid, how to work better, and some other issues, like guild removal of persons.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3707">Capias</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/4/2002 - 10:07 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2989">Capias Maximus</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														My 2c: I don't have the experience that some of you guys have at this game.  But the way I saw it, we overreached our bounds.  We are -not- Dragon's Fist, and we shouldn't raid like we were.  IMO for our next raid we should pick areas that we know we can own, rather than traveling further on in search of bigger mobs and phatter lewt.  Our bear group was overmatched where we were stationed.  We might have held with 6, but even then it would have been dicey.  I don't know about you higher groups, except that in a few minutes after I came up to the castle you all got wiped in what looked like an overpull (and my @#$! camo ran out at the wrong time).  If the entire higher level group had stayed together near the castle entrance, and both lower level groups had stayed in the graveyard together, I think we might have had real success.  <br />
<br />
I don't know if I'll make the next meeting or not.  Seems like alot of work to meet all in one location, when we can talk stuff out in /gu without moving.  Seems like we could even use the message board to discuss things, like we are doing in this thread.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3554">Horadur</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/4/2002 - 12:37 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2850">Horadur Horaroar</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2851">Kzudx</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I agree that meetings shouldn't have a set place to go, we can easily get things decided in /gu while getting XP.<br />
Another thing is, we only had the one group head up to the castle and IMHO we should have had everyone stick together, maybe with both enchanters there mezzing and more people to hold the mobs we could have made it farther into the castle, and then fought our way back out.<br />
<br />
I still need my hilt and bone from Mistmoore, so I hope this dosen't mean we aren't going to try again in a few weeks						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3111">ktadema</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/4/2002 - 4:26 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2488">Givins Ntakhiens</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2861">Felious Gudlious</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2487">Izzek Krakumheads</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Capias, I hate to agree with you, but yeah, I think maybe we were trying to bite off more than we could chew.  I wanted to think we could take that graveyard, and we might not have QUITE had the guns to do it.  <br />
<br />
I agree with something else you said:  I like using this forum as a place to vent and talk things over.  I know for me, I'm a working boy, and my game time is limited.  I hate to use my game time for meeting.  Now Guildsay is different!  I can get on here while I'm at work and talk about the guild.  So to me.....Guildsay's message boards are an EXCELLENT place to take care of beaurocracy and red tape.  I hope that more of the guild will post more on here.  Good to see you on here Horadur and Wurog!!!						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3548">olthar</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/5/2002 - 9:59 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2836">Olthar Othlinden</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2837">Tylendil</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I agree that I also hate to use gametime for a meeting, but sometimes it is necessary, not everyone is on that message board, and even less actually use it. The reason for going to one area to meet is simply everyone else does it why not us. It allows us to get to meet everyone else in the guild, and have some fun. If we did a meeting in guildsay then people would be fighting and would miss parts of the meeting, which would not work too well. I also agree that we bit off more than we could chew in MistMoore, which is why a good part of the meeting will be &quot;where are we raiding next&quot; it should not be too long of a meeting, we don't have much to discuss, unless anyone else has stuff to add to my ajenda. (spelled wrong as usual)						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=2690">Bickelhaupt</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/6/2002 - 7:37 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2143">Bickelhaupt</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2578">Scandyl</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														If you guys decide to try MM again let me know.  With a little notice I can try to have Bickelhaupt (53 cleric) parked there to help with healing and rezzes						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3548">olthar</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/6/2002 - 8:37 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2836">Olthar Othlinden</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2837">Tylendil</a></div>					
